Lake now detects its explicit installation and `lake clean` succeeds; the remaining failure is Lean’s own executable-path lookup. I’m testing the minimal sandbox-safe repair: a byte-identical copy of the pinned `lean` launcher under `/tmp/audit-work`, with its libraries still read directly from the pinned toolchain. This changes only the execution location, not the compiler or libraries.
